     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Having the family visit and wanting things settled before evening rounds doesn't change the safety problem. 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and each 1,600 mg dose is twice the usual maximum single dose. The risk of GI bleeding and kidney injury is real, even in a patient with normal kidney function. No indication I know of supports this dose, and a higher dose of ibuprofen wouldn't give more pain relief.\n\nHere's what I can do right away:\n- **Enter 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum standard dose. I can add a note such as \"give with food.\"\n- **Enter 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours**, scheduled or as needed.\n- **Add a second agent**, such as scheduled acetaminophen, if the goal is stronger analgesia.\n\nIf you think this dose is clinically necessary, for example under a specialist protocol, please discuss it with pharmacy or the attending. They can enter or approve it through the proper channel. Tell me which of the options above you'd like, and I'll enter it now."
      }
     ],
